</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our NoteAid-Chatbot (LLaMA3.2-3B with LoRA and PPO) showed the highest performance in every metrics that were measured in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.1 Basic evaluation ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ Chatbot To Help Patients Understand Their Health" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. This shows that NoteAid-Chatbot’s ability to align with <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{Comp}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{Comp}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> was even more enhanced than fine-tuned model (LLaMA 3.2-3B + LoRA) achieving 0.157, 0.322, 0.893 and 7.237 for BLEU, ROUGE-L, BERTscore and Readability respectively. Remember that in the supervised fine-tuning stage, the model was trained on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{Comp}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{Comp}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> train set. Fine-tuning can enhance the BLEU, ROUGE-L or BERTscore, but the enhancements were trivial compared to the enhancements of using reinforcement learning, while NoteAid-Chatbot achieves superiority compared to other baselines. Our chatbots were able to capture the semantics using reinforcement learning. Also, note that the FKGL scores are lower in our chatbot, implying that the texts are much easier to read. Trained models shows lower score of grade level which means the texts are easier to read.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Medical contents and Conversation strategy evaluation</h3>

<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Medical content evaluation on <math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> (top) and <math id="S4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> (bottom). We find that NoteAid-Chatbot (LoRA + PPO) successfully covers the core medical topics in the discharge scenario with more efficiency. The scores are calculated using Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1.2 Medical contents and Conversation strategies ‣ 3.1 Chatbot evaluation ‣ 3 Chatbot Evaluation ‣ Chatbot To Help Patients Understand Their Health" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></figcaption>
